---
name: scljet-large-page
description: a 4096-byte page survives a byte-slice update on every lane, including JS (no TCO)
backends: [int, js]
---

# A 4096-byte page must not overflow the JS stack

`copyLoop` in `scljet/bytes.ssc` used to recurse once per byte of the slice, so a 4096-byte page went
4096 frames deep and JS died with `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded`, while 512 stayed
shallow and every other lane tolerated it by trampolining
(`BUGS.md` `scljet-js-large-page-byteslice-recursion-overflow`).

**The page size is the assertion.** Every other scljet case uses 512 precisely because 4096 crashed;
this one uses 4096 on purpose, so a return to per-byte recursion fails here rather than silently
limiting what page sizes the engine supports.

[ByteSlice, SqliteValue, SqlInteger, SqlText, buildTableDatabase](std/scljet/index.ssc)
[executeMutation, queryImage](std/scljet/sql.ssc)

```scalascript
def showValue(v: SqliteValue): String = v match
  case SqlInteger(x) => x.toString
  case SqlText(x) => x
  case _ => "?"

def showRow(row: List[SqliteValue]): String = row match
  case Nil => ""
  case h :: Nil => showValue(h)
  case h :: t => showValue(h) + "|" + showRow(t)

def showRows(rows: List[List[SqliteValue]]): String = rows match
  case Nil => "(none)"
  case h :: Nil => showRow(h)
  case h :: t => showRow(h) + " ; " + showRows(t)

buildTableDatabase(4096, 1, 1, "emp", "CREATE TABLE emp(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT)",
  List(List(SqlInteger(1L), SqlText("ann")))) match
  case Left(error) => println("build failed: " + error.message)
  case Right(base) =>
    // The INSERT is what drives copyLoop across the whole page.
    executeMutation(base, "INSERT INTO emp VALUES (2, 'bob')") match
      case Left(message) => println("insert failed: " + message)
      case Right(next) =>
        queryImage(next, "SELECT id, name FROM emp") match
          case Left(message) => println("query failed: " + message)
          case Right(rows) => println(showRows(rows))
```
